 "result": "I created two files in the repository root. I could not build or run the image, so it is untested.\n\n- **`Dockerfile`**: a three-stage build that follows the project's `npm start` flow.\n  - It builds the React frontend with `react-scripts build`.\n  - It installs backend production dependencies with `npm ci --omit=dev`.\n  - It runs `node -r dotenv/config server.js` with `NODE_ENV=PRODUCTION`, so Express serves `frontend/build` alongside the API. The server listens on port 3002 by default.\n- **`.dockerignore`**: excludes `.git`, `.env` and `.env.*`, `node_modules`, `frontend/build`, logs, docs, and `assets/`.\n\nChoices I made:\n- **Node 22** (`bookworm-slim`), since Node 20 reached end of life in April 2026. The version is an `ARG`, so it is easy to change.\n- **The image runs as the non-root `node` user.**\n- **`.env` is excluded from the image.** Pass configuration at run time with `docker run -e KEY=value`, or with an env file that uses `KEY=value` lines. The repo's `.env` uses `KEY = value` spacing, which Docker's env-file parser may not accept.\n- **No startup script.** `server_bootup.sh` only chains the same steps the Dockerfile does, so I did not add a copy.\n\nRun-time variables, from `.env.example`:\n- `SERVICE_URL` is needed for the default quote source. Without it, requests that do not use `quoteCategory` or a custom `quotesUrl` will fail.\n- `UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY` is optional and only needed for `bgSource=unsplash`.\n\nFiles created:\n- `/home/user/work/runs/zhravan__github-readme-quotes/haiku/ws/Dockerfile`\n- `/home/user/work/runs/zhravan__github-readme-quotes/haiku/ws/.dockerignore`",
